<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX2-QA-009>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX2-QA-009" ;
  triage:title "No mechanical boundary test guards the Herdr .prompt() call site against a future direct call from HerdrQueueWakePump" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs has a precedent for this class of check (herdr_constructors_have_one_composition_root_call_site) but does not cover .prompt( calls; nothing enforces that HerdrQueueWakePump reaches .prompt() only via the selector/emitter routing. Current code is correct; this is a lint-gap. Fix: add a boundary_enforcement.rs test asserting the production .prompt( call sites are limited to the received_hook_selector emitter (and the adapter impls). Reported by ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-F002 (minor) on PR #1186 QA-1 (head 4f77d2fff)." ;
